Subject: [PATCH] 5413: the case-details panel gets a case description (switch
 off)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Giorgi's 5413: the details panel says in two or three plain sentences what
the case is about — what the owner wants, for whom, where it stands. The
goal's brief cannot be shown as it is (the assistant's working notes, tool
names and timings; a third of goals have none; median 554 characters), so
after each run on a goal's conversation the server writes the description
from the title, the brief and the latest lines, keeps it only when it is two
or three plain sentences with no number or tool name, stores it
(threads.case_description, migration 245), returns it in GET /threads and
sends it as thread_updated.

The writing prompt is new model-facing text: CASE_DESCRIPTION_ON is false
until Misho's yes on its exact words (D44).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01HwFREQwL5g9E6qRrUf9bau
